    S2(S2(A("a"), A("a")), S2(A("b"), A("b"))))),
DEF("case:abs-targets-unsorted", S2(A("rmap:abs_targets"),
    S2(S2(A("F1"), A("T9")), S2(A("F2"), A("T1"))))),
DEF("case:abs-targets-empty", S2(A("rmap:abs_targets"), PHI())),

"store:drop_named and store:replace_cell against with_watermark_native (main.rs). replace_cell is the REMOVE-ALL-THEN-APPEND-LAST discipline, which is NOT Backus 13.3.4's pop-then-push that define_in uses -- that one removes only the FIRST match and PREPENDS, so the two must not be conflated and the -replaces case pins which. That -replaces and -appends answer identically is the upsert property itself: whether the name was already there stops being observable. drop-named-all answers phi, the arm a filter written as a guard gets wrong.",
